# LTI deliverable content checklist

Applies to Markdown under `LTI-<INITIALS>/` (main design doc and `prompts.md`).

## Main design document (`LTI-<INITIALS>.md`)

Ensure the single consolidated document includes:

1. **Brief description** of LTI software, added value, and competitive advantages.  
2. **Main functions** explained clearly.  
3. **Lean Canvas** diagram (business model) — embed or link; describe how to read it.  
4. **Three main use cases** — narrative for each **plus** an associated diagram per use case.  
5. **Data model** — entities, attributes (name **and** type), and relationships.  
6. **High-level system design** — prose **and** a diagram.  
7. **C4 diagram** — one component drilled into in depth (any component the author chooses).

Use Mermaid, embedded images, or links to diagrams in repo-friendly formats. Keep diagrams legible when rendered on GitHub.

## `prompts.md`

- Capture **prompts actually used** with assistants (ChatGPT, Gemini, Copilot, Claude, etc.).  
- Organize for readability (e.g. by artifact or phase).  
- Do not omit this file; it is part of the graded deliverable per course instructions.

## Language

Course materials are EN/ES; **deliverable language** may follow instructor preference or student choice unless specified otherwise — stay consistent within one folder.
